-- The Palladium RPG Book II: Old Ones - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 9 creatures (migration 074) and 144 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~179-old-ones-people-and-monsters.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 2 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.
--
-- THIS IS THE 1984 FIRST-EDITION BOOK. Nate, 2026-10-05: people only (the
-- three classes stay out), every full stat block, a named being is a notable
-- NPC and a kind of monster is a creature, and the one-line residents of the
-- Place of Magic (printed 176-196) fold into their kind rather than become
-- rows. Every bonuses_note opens by saying the figures are first edition and
-- every description closes the same way. No personal S.D.C. or P.P.E. is
-- entered because the book prints none; an armour's S.D.C. is with the armour.
--
-- Read from page renders throughout: the text layer of this book is welded,
-- glyph-corrupt and digit-substituted, so no name or number came from it.
-- book-reconcile checked every row against the renders, by section.










-- Read the result back. This script asserts its OWN rows and nothing else.
SELECT 'all 9 creatures are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 9 AS want
  FROM creatures WHERE slug IN ('serpent-beast', 'mystic-spider', 'monster-toad', 'serpent-man', 'pseudo-demon-guard', 'low-caste-pseudo-demon', 'tomb-worm', 'minotaur-old-ones', 'zombie-of-artimus');
SELECT 'and 0 of them are playable' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 0 AS want
  FROM creatures WHERE playable = 1 AND slug IN ('serpent-beast', 'mystic-spider', 'monster-toad', 'serpent-man', 'pseudo-demon-guard', 'low-caste-pseudo-demon', 'tomb-worm', 'minotaur-old-ones', 'zombie-of-artimus');
SELECT 'all 144 notable NPCs are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 144 AS want
